{
  "comment": "The cases of the interface contract that give every argument of a member that takes a `Pages`, without faults, files or a service, in the case form of binding (G-5). A generated test that checks one argument of such a member takes its `Pages` from the first such case of the member (binding GN-13t), because the core refuses a `Pages` of placeholder arguments with invalid_application before it reads the argument under test (HY-2.9). Each case gives the smallest application that routes the request GET / to its page home, whose region content keeps no value. The group route routes that request to the page (HY-116). The group kept gives no value for a path that the region does not keep (HY-40.1). The group keep answers 403 to a request to the kept endpoint without the token of the form (HY-24.4). The group request makes the page request of the route home. The group register registers a function of the application on such a `Pages` (HYC-24.9), so that a generated test that needs any instance of `Pages`, as B-5c does, takes it from this case and not from placeholder arguments (binding GN-13t).",
